-- Ring 4: The Thermodynamic Freeze — Cramer-Rao and Self-Concordance
---------------------------------------------------------------

/- The Cramer-Rao lower inequality:
   For any unbiased estimator θ̂ of parameter θ, the covariance satisfies:
     Cov(θ̂) ≥ I(θ)^{-1}
   where I(θ) is the Fisher information matrix.

   In a chiral-style information-geometric model, I(θ) can be compared
   with the Bures metric tensor g_{ij}. The Cramer-Rao inequality then
   provides a statistical limit for estimation precision.

   As the number of measurements N → ∞:
   - The parameter estimate freezes onto the true value
   - The covariance approaches the Cramer-Rao scale
   - The parameter space may show sharp limiting behavior
   - The statistical manifold can be approximated geometrically

   Comparable language can be useful when discussing:
   - γ-ray spectroscopy with millions of coincidences
   - LLM training with billions of tokens
   - cosmological cooling models -/


